course: dictionary
lesson: 14730
title: Progression: moving step by step
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A progression is a movement from one stage to the next, step by step. You can see it in a caterpillar that becomes a butterfly, or in a player who gets better each season. «The progression from caterpillar to butterfly» shows the stages in order, one after another.
explain: Progression also has special meanings in maths and music. «3, 6, 9, 12» is an arithmetic progression, because you add 3 each time. «2, 4, 8, 16» is a geometric progression, because you multiply by 2 each time. In music, «a chord progression» is a row of chords played one after another.
explain: Look for clue words to find the meaning: step, stage, rule, next, over time. They tell you that progression is about things happening in order. When you see a number pattern, ask yourself: what rule links one number to the next?
fact: Progression means moving forward step by step, from one stage to the next.
fact: «The progression from caterpillar to butterfly» shows the stages in order.
fact: An arithmetic progression adds the same number each time, such as 3, 6, 9, 12.
fact: A geometric progression multiplies by the same number each time, such as 2, 4, 8, 16.
fact: Progression can also mean getting better or worse over time, as in «her progression in swimming».
exercise: In «the progression from caterpillar to butterfly», what is the progression? | *Moving step by step from one stage to the next | A kind of insect | A sudden jump straight to the end | A sad ending
exercise: What is the rule in the number pattern 4, 8, 12, 16? | Multiply by 2 each time | The numbers are chosen at random | Subtract 1 each time | *Add 4 each time
exercise: Is 2, 4, 8, 16 an arithmetic progression or a geometric progression? | Neither, because it has no rule | An arithmetic progression, because it adds 2 each time | A chord progression, because it is played on a piano | *A geometric progression, because it multiplies by 2 each time
test: Which sentence uses progression to mean getting better over time? | *«Her reading showed steady progression all year.» | «The dog barked at the postman.» | «The number 10 is even.»
test: What is the next number in the arithmetic progression 5, 10, 15, 20? | 21 | 30 | 24 | *25
exam: Which phrase names a series of chords played one after another? | caterpillar stage | *chord progression | geometric progression | arithmetic progression
